{"id": "EUVD-2026-101755", "enisaUuid": "6bff270a-24f6-380b-a3f3-f94af9b246fa", "description": "Nodemailer from 3.0.0 before 10.0.10 contains a quadratic complexity denial of service vulnerability in the SMTP client reply parser in SMTPConnection._onData and isPartialResponse. A malicious SMTP server or on-path attacker can stream continuation lines without a completion line before authentication, blocking the Node.js event loop and exhausting memory.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T22:53:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T13:30:56", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/nodemailer/nodemailer/security/advisories/GHSA-4g23-2xm8-66gc", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nodemailer-3.0.0-before-10.0.10-denial-of-service-via-smtp-reply-parsing"], "aliases": ["GHSA-37fc-hcrp-mmff", "CVE-2026-110872"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7c200423-5b2d-3729-a6a2-83b77a429da3", "product": {"name": "nodemailer", "vendor": {"name": "nodemailer"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 <10.0.10"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "da72bae2-0908-3d82-a274-950fd1411d1d", "vendor": {"name": "nodemailer"}}], "isExploited": false}